preConditionHook:
// EL: pairHigh = MaxList(high[1], high[2]); pairLow = MinList(low[1], low[2]);
// and the entry test close[2] < open[2] and close[1] > open[1] and
// close[1] - open[1] >= bodyFraction * (high[1] - low[1]) and close > pairHigh.
//
// Entering beyond BOTH bars of the reversal pair is the whole point: it avoids
// the one-tick trap at the signal bar's extreme, and it makes this a different
// trigger bar from TwoBarReversal, which fires on the pair itself.
//
// MaxList / MinList select among high[1] / high[2] and low[1] / low[2] -- tick
// grid PRICE operands, the scope the ACCEPTED register row allows, where the
// two candidates differ by zero or by at least one tick (1e9-1e11 times the
// 2.22e-12 relational tolerance), so which comparison the selection carries
// cannot matter and a plain > / < stands in. AverageUpperTailFraction does the
// same for its body-top selection.
//
// The selections persist across bars as class members, so both are assigned
// unconditionally every bar rather than left over from the last one.
pairHigh = high[1];
if (high[2] > pairHigh) pairHigh = high[2];
pairLow = low[1];
if (low[2] < pairLow) pairLow = low[2];
